TASK 4

Given a food delivery fraud detection system:

TP = 40
TN = 150
FP = 20
FN = 10

Calculate the F1 Score.

CODE:

tp = 40
tn = 150
fp = 20
fn = 10

# Calculate precision
precision = tp / (tp + fp)

# Calculate recall
recall = tp / (tp + fn)

# Calculate F1 score
f1 = 2 * (precision * recall) / (precision + recall)

print("Precision:", precision)
print("Recall:", recall)
print("F1 Score:", f1)
print("F1 Score (%):", f1 * 100)


CALCULATION:

Precision:

= 40 / (40 + 20)
= 40 / 60
= 0.6667


Recall:

= 40 / (40 + 10)
= 40 / 50
= 0.8


F1 Score:

= 2 * (0.6667 * 0.8) / (0.6667 + 0.8)

= 0.7273

F1 Score = 72.73%


EXPLANATION:

The F1 score combines precision and recall into a single value, so a higher F1 score indicates a better balance between correctly detecting fraud and avoiding false fraud alerts.


